# Build context hygiene.
#
# The wasm and the target directory are the two big things that would otherwise be sent to
# the daemon and then thrown away: `target/` alone is several gigabytes, and `web/web/ui/pkg`
# is regenerated inside the image.

target/
**/target/

# Regenerated by the build, and stale copies here would be silently shipped instead.
web/web/ui/pkg/

# The Tauri build output and its generated permission schemas.
desktop/gen/

# The public deployment's own state: the compose file, the Caddyfile, the two client builds
# the server hands out and its volume archives. `deploy/compose.yaml` mounts each of those at
# run time, so none of it is build input — and the downloads alone are tens of megabytes that
# would otherwise be copied into a layer nothing reads.
deploy/

# Vendored toolchain bootstrap and a local cargo home, if the developer has them here.
.tools/
.cargo/
.rust/

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/

# Node and documentation are not needed to build the server or the portal.
node_modules/
docs/

# A local database must never end up inside an image.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
